99
00:06:52,521 --> 00:06:57,520
Temperatures inside can reach 1,000 degrees Fahrenheit.

100
00:06:57,521 --> 00:07:01,020
We're actually inside a furnace used to test walls.

101
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:06,460
We install doors, windows, even glass-blocked walls in this furnace

102
00:07:06,461 --> 00:07:11,940
and then burn it from one side to make sure the wall can withstand the intense heat of a fire.

103
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:16,520
UL Torch has more than 100 walls every year,

104
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:22,960
and its tests extend to walls made of materials you wouldn't think could catch fire, like concrete.

105
00:07:22,961 --> 00:07:27,860
What we're seeing is a wall coming out of our furnace

106
00:07:27,861 --> 00:07:30,620
