509
00:32:55,181 --> 00:32:58,440
The conspirators were Frank Morris, Clarence Anglin,

510
00:32:58,441 --> 00:33:01,420
and his brother John.

511
00:33:01,421 --> 00:33:04,680
Their starting point was to gain access to the utility corridor

512
00:33:04,681 --> 00:33:07,180
by secretly digging through the cell walls surrounding

513
00:33:07,181 --> 00:33:09,600
the ventilators.

514
00:33:09,601 --> 00:33:13,600
The walls were nine inches thick, but the steel reinforced

515
00:33:13,601 --> 00:33:18,900
concrete had been weakened by San Francisco's salty, damp air.

516
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:23,540
The deterioration continues to this day.

517
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:26,340
The salt environment on Alcatraz is very harsh

518
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:27,940
on anything that's metal.

519
00:33:28,040 --> 00:33:30,660
And of course, in the foundation of a lot of these structures,

520
00:33:30,760 --> 00:33:34,260
they have metal I-beams that are rusting and expanding.

521
00:33:34,360 --> 00:33:37,060
And when they rust and expand, it's like a cancer.

522
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,500
It pops the concrete off.

523
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:40,400
And it's happening all around Alcatraz.

524
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:48,900
Another factor inside the walls weakened the concrete further,

525
00:33:50,120 --> 00:33:51,740
substandard construction methods.

526
00:33:53,340 --> 00:33:56,800
The cell house had been built in 1909 as a military prison,

527
00:33:58,100 --> 00:34:01,540
using materials left over from the army outpost that predated it.

528
00:34:02,220 --> 00:34:05,060
Instead of using a lot of rock in this concrete,

529
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:07,360
you're supposed to use good washed river rock.

530
00:34:07,760 --> 00:34:10,120
They used ground up brick, broken brick,

531
00:34:10,180 --> 00:34:12,200
from the old fortifications on Alcatraz.

532
00:34:12,201 --> 00:34:16,100
What the brick did is it was porous, and it wicked in water,

533
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:20,060
especially seawater and San Francisco fog,

534
00:34:20,640 --> 00:34:25,980
and that would lead to the metal inside starting to corrode, to rust.

535
00:34:27,460 --> 00:34:30,480
Morris and the Anglin brothers took advantage of the deficiencies

536
00:34:30,481 --> 00:34:33,920
inside Alcatraz's walls as they launched their daring plan.

537
00:34:35,040 --> 00:34:40,660
With stolen drill bits, they were able to drill holes into the wall,

538
00:34:40,661 --> 00:34:43,540
a hole here, a hole here, a hole here.

539
00:34:43,760 --> 00:34:45,300
And every time they drilled one of the holes,

540
00:34:45,460 --> 00:34:47,540
they would fill it in with soap and tissue paper

541
00:34:47,541 --> 00:34:50,860
and paint, you know, from just paint stocks.

542
00:34:50,960 --> 00:34:52,300
The guys were allowed to paint their own cells.

543
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:54,520
Pretty much blend in with the rest of the wall.

544
00:34:55,040 --> 00:34:58,120
When they were ready to finally remove the wall pre-weakened,

545
00:34:58,680 --> 00:35:00,640
then it could be kicked out.

546
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:05,260
On June 11th, the night of the escape,

547
00:35:05,261 --> 00:35:12,820
The inmates placed dummy heads in their beds to convince the guards they were asleep.

548
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:16,640
Then they wriggled through the openings into the utility corridor

549
00:35:16,641 --> 00:35:21,440
and positioned cardboard replicas of the ventilators over the holes.

550
00:35:23,200 --> 00:35:29,860
From here, they went up the spider web of plumbing, pretty much just like a jungle gym.

551
00:35:30,180 --> 00:35:32,160
They made their way to the top of the cell house.

552
00:35:32,161 --> 00:35:36,500
They climbed into a hollow ventilator

553
00:35:36,600 --> 00:35:40,100
and out onto the last ventilator opening that got them

554
00:35:40,200 --> 00:35:43,000
onto the roof of the cell house itself.

555
00:35:43,100 --> 00:35:45,400
X marks the spot where the three convicts

556
00:35:45,500 --> 00:35:48,400
climbed through the utility corridor to access the roof.

557
00:35:48,500 --> 00:35:51,920
They popped an air van off, ran across this roof,

558
00:35:52,020 --> 00:35:55,520
slid down a set of water pipes, and entered the water

559
00:35:55,620 --> 00:35:56,920
at the north end of the island.

560
00:35:56,921 --> 00:36:00,420
Island.

561
00:36:00,421 --> 00:36:03,060
The next morning, prison officials were shocked

562
00:36:03,061 --> 00:36:05,880
to discover the three men missing,

563
00:36:05,881 --> 00:36:10,220
finding only the ingenious artifacts of their escape.

564
00:36:10,221 --> 00:36:12,320
The convicts were never seen again.

565
00:36:12,321 --> 00:36:15,280
The suspicion is that they drowned

566
00:36:15,281 --> 00:36:18,680
and their bodies were swept out to sea and just not recovered.

567
00:36:18,681 --> 00:36:21,280
But you've got to add that the FBI considers the case

568
00:36:21,281 --> 00:36:22,620
to be still open, and they're still

569
00:36:22,621 --> 00:36:26,620
wanted for an escape from the federal penitentiary.

570
00:36:26,621 --> 00:36:30,300
Whatever their fate, three men outside the law

571
00:36:30,301 --> 00:36:33,580
earned a place in history by going inside the walls.

572
00:36:37,220 --> 00:36:40,100
Today, innovative tech inside your walls

573
00:36:40,101 --> 00:36:46,380
can help you escape as well from ever increasing energy bills.

